/-! # Stabilization of a closed inverse system of algebraic spaces

Source: Stacks Project, Limits of Spaces, Tag 0828,
Lemma `lemma-finite-type-eventually-closed`, clause (3), with Y equal to the limit X
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-closed-limit-stabilization).

The diagram and its limit cone are taken in algebraic spaces over B. Quasi-compactness
is the existence of a quasi-compact scheme atlas, closed immersions use scheme tests,
and local finite type and presentation use the existing compatible étale chart tests.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace

/-- A locally finitely presented limit over B of quasi-compact spaces locally of finite
type over B, with closed immersion transitions, has isomorphic projections at every
sufficiently large stage.

Source: Stacks Project, Limits of Spaces, Tag 0828(3), with Y = X
(blueprint: lem-sfb-space-closed-limit-stabilization).

Proof, following the six steps of the accepted node:
1. Choose a stage a and restrict to its directed tail. A tail cone extends uniquely
   to every index by passing to a common upper bound, so the limit is unchanged.
   Apply lem-sfb-space-relative-lfp-permanence to C → C_a → B: the composite is locally
   finitely presented and the second map is locally of finite type, so C → C_a is
   locally finitely presented.
2. Choose an affine surjective étale atlas U_a → C_a using
   lem-trf-space-qc-finite-affine-atlas-refinement. Each U_i = C_i ×_(C_a) U_a is a
   closed subscheme of U_a by def-weil-closed-immersion and hence affine and
   quasi-compact by lem-weil-pbc-affine-scheme-qcqs. Its map to U_a is locally of
   finite type since a quotient algebra is generated by the empty set. The same
   scheme tests show that the transitions U_j → U_i are closed immersions.
3. Closed immersions are affine. Apply lem-sfb-space-affine-limits-schematic-stages:
   the sheaf limit is C, its projection to C_a is affine, and
   U = C ×_(C_a) U_a = lim U_i is an affine scheme. Yoneda identifies scheme maps
   with maps of the corresponding representable sheaves
   (def-trf-scheme-algebraic-space), so this is also the limit in schemes.
4. Apply lem-sfb-space-local-properties-chart-test to C → C_a with target chart U_a
   and the identity source chart of U. It gives local finite presentation of U → U_a.
5. Apply lem-weil-pbc-closed-limit-lfp-stabilization to the schemes U_i over U_a.
   Their quasi-compactness, local finite type, closed transitions and locally finitely
   presented limit were checked in steps 2–4. Obtain i₀ such that U → U_i is an
   isomorphism for every i ≥ i₀.
6. For such i, lem-trf-space-fibre-products-etale-covers makes U_i → C_i surjective
   étale, and the pullback of C → C_i is U → U_i. On every scheme test, this is an
   fppf cover (def-weil-etale-morphism and def-pc-fppf-site). The unique local lift
   to C agrees on the double overlap and glues uniquely by the fppf sheaf axiom
   (def-trf-algebraic-space). These lifts give the inverse to C → C_i. -/
theorem exists_isIso_projection_of_closed_limit_locallyOfFinitePresentation
    {S : Scheme.{u}} (B : AlgebraicSpace S)
    {I : Type u} [Preorder I] [IsDirected I (· ≤ ·)] [Nonempty I]
    (D : Iᵒᵖ ⥤ Over B)
    (hqc : ∀ i : Iᵒᵖ, ∃ (U : Over S) (a : yoneda.obj U ⟶ (D.obj i).left.obj.obj),
      CompactSpace U.left ∧ IsEtale a ∧ IsSurjective a)
    (hlft : ∀ i : Iᵒᵖ, MapIsLocally (@LocallyOfFiniteType) (D.obj i).hom)
    (hclosed : ∀ {i j : Iᵒᵖ} (f : i ⟶ j),
      IsRepresentableWith (fun _ _ p ↦ IsClosedImmersion p.left) (D.map f).left.hom.hom)
    (c : Cone D) (hc : IsLimit c)
    (hlfp : MapIsLocallyOfFinitePresentation c.pt.hom) :
    ∃ i₀ : I, ∀ i : I, i₀ ≤ i → IsIso (c.π.app (op i)).left := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.AlgebraicSpace
